haracter clipping through a wall on one platform but not another—it’s treated as a critical bug and patched immediately. ### **So Why Do You “Never See” a Difference?** Because: - Developers **actively seek out and fix** any perceptible disparities during QA. - The remaining differences are **below the noise floor** of human reaction time and visual acuity. - The **game feel** (response time, movement, aiming) is tuned to match the player’s expectations, not to be scientifically identical. In short: the differences exist, but they are engineered to be **indistinguishable to the human playing the game**. You trust your perception, and the industry works hard to maintain that trust. If a game *did* feel different, players would complain loudly—and they do, when ports are bad. So the fact that you don’t see differences is actually evidence of how well this engineering works.
